-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Conclusion
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Each twin's anchors are independently protected. Reverting either one alone
turns 6 checks red; neither mutation is silent any more. Coverage is
symmetric by construction -- per pattern field there is one .ps1-only check,
one .sh-only check, and one cross-twin parity check -- so a single-twin
regression is attributed to the twin that caused it.

The three paired newline-free controls stayed green under BOTH mutations,
which is what rules out the block passing by rejecting everything.

Both twins restored and verified byte-identical after the runs.
